  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I have three files: an expression matrix of 15,000 genes by 90 muscle biopsies, a design table with one row per biopsy giving age, sex coded 0/1 and sequencing batch coded 0/1, and a gene annotation table mapping Ensembl IDs to symbols. I want to know which parts of the gene co-expression are associated with age while accounting for batch and sex."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"which parts of the gene co-expression are associated with age while accounting for batch and sex\" -- available from COBRA.\n\nSelected path: **COBRA**.\n\n**COBRA** — Model covariate-associated gene co-expression with COBRA. COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Correcting gene means alone may leave covariance confounding. Covariate-associated components are not TF-to-gene regulatory edges or proof that a covariate causes the expression pattern.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `expression_file`: expression matrix\n- `design_file`: sample covariate design matrix\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `coexpression_network`: Inferred gene-to-gene associations.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nThis is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
